{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890224",
      "title": "Working with refs & useRef",
      "sourceHash": "d9b834055a0556e4e535968e77b99b7827bbbf00ce8bf96d335d37b46ebce266",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.5,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Now, we learned how we can use refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 6.89,
          "en": "in a functional component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.89,
          "end": 11.563,
          "en": "We can import the useRef hook here from react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.49,
          "end": 13.57,
          "en": "And once we did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.57,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "we can create a ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 20.33,
          "en": "like the todoTextInputRef here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.28,
          "end": 23.33,
          "en": "and we call useRef like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.33,
          "end": 25.253,
          "en": "to create such a reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 29.8,
          "en": "Then we can go to the HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.8,
          "end": 32.09,
          "en": "to which you wanna connect the ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.09,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "typically an input element or a text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 40.74,
          "en": "And we set the special ref property on that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.74,
          "end": 42.64,
          "en": "and point at our ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.64,
          "end": 45.65,
          "en": "In this case, we point at todoTextInputRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.95,
          "end": 51.26,
          "en": "Now, if I do that, you see I get an error down there though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.26,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "Again with a very long text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 58.403,
          "en": "that in the end ref is receiving the wrong type of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "Now, ref wants a ref created with useRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "that's not wrong, but we're not explicit enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "about the ref we're creating here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 71.08,
          "en": "In vanilla JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.08,
          "end": 73.69,
          "en": "this code works because we don't have the concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.69,
          "end": 75.763,
          "en": "of extra type annotations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.61,
          "end": 79.01,
          "en": "But when working with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.01,
          "end": 83.11,
          "en": "TypeScript actually wants to know a bit more about our ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.11,
          "end": 85.61,
          "en": "When we create it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.61,
          "end": 87.76,
          "en": "TypeScript actually has no idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.76,
          "end": 91.33,
          "en": "that we eventually will connect it to a input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.33,
          "end": 93.363,
          "en": "That's only clear down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.57,
          "end": 96.78999999999999,
          "en": "But since it's not clear in this line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.78999999999999,
          "end": 99.97,
          "en": "we could use this ref in any possible way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.97,
          "end": 103.77000000000001,
          "en": "We can connect it to any HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 106.21000000000001,
          "en": "And that's, in the end, the kind of error we get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.21000000000001,
          "end": 108.83,
          "en": "We're passing a ref as a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.83,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "to this input that is not clearly focused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 114.78999999999999,
          "en": "on this kind of HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.303,
          "en": "This could also be a ref that wants a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.39,
          "end": 121.34,
          "en": "So we have to be more explicit about the kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.34,
          "end": 125.9,
          "en": "of data we will store in this ref eventually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.9,
          "end": 129.34,
          "en": "And we do this again with a generic type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.34,
          "end": 134.34,
          "en": "That's why useRef actually is a generic type out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.72,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "We can add the angled brackets here now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 141.82999999999998,
          "en": "to explicitly set the concrete type of ref we wanna create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.82999999999998,
          "end": 143.69,
          "en": "in this instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.69,
          "end": 147.57999999999998,
          "en": "So ref, useRef is able to work with all kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.57999999999998,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "of data we will store in this ref here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 155.8,
          "en": "all kinds of HTML objects we could connect with this ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.8,
          "end": 159.82999999999998,
          "en": "but we now have to specify which concrete value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.1,
          "en": "or HTML element we plan",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.1,
          "end": 165.65,
          "en": "on storing into this specific ref object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.65,
          "end": 167.853,
          "en": "we are creating here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.76,
          "end": 172.31,
          "en": "And here I know that I wanna store such a input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.31,
          "end": 174.79,
          "en": "and that has a built-in type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.79,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "And that's the HTMLInputElement type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 183.2,
          "en": "All those DOM elements have built-in types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.2,
          "end": 185.77,
          "en": "which you can use in TypeScript to refer to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.77,
          "end": 188.74,
          "en": "and for the input, it's the HTMLInputElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.74,
          "end": 191.48,
          "en": "For a button, it would be the HTMLButtonElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.48,
          "end": 195.08,
          "en": "For a paragraph, it would be the HTMLParagraphElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.08,
          "end": 196.193,
          "en": "And so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.11,
          "end": 200.52,
          "en": "You can also always visit the MDN page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.52,
          "end": 203.119,
          "en": "of an element, like here the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.119,
          "end": 205.61,
          "en": "And even though that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.61,
          "end": 208.185,
          "en": "is not focusing on TypeScript at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.185,
          "end": 212.44,
          "en": "on that page, you will find information like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.44,
          "end": 216.28,
          "en": "Like here you find that the input element is based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.28,
          "end": 220.023,
          "en": "on the HTMLInputElement interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 225.4,
          "en": "And that's why we use that as a type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.4,
          "end": 227.44,
          "en": "So now we are making it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.44,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "that the ref we're creating here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "will actually be connected to an HTMLInputElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.19,
          "end": 236.72,
          "en": "But I'm still getting an error down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.72,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "And we're getting this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.75,
          "en": "because actually we have to set a default value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.75,
          "end": 244.34,
          "en": "because this ref could already be a sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.34,
          "end": 246.71,
          "en": "to some other element maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.71,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "out of the box by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 251.81,
          "en": "And that's why we should provide a starting value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.81,
          "end": 253.42,
          "en": "and at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.42,
          "end": 254.74,
          "en": "we have no connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.74,
          "end": 257.74,
          "en": "and therefore, the starting value is null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.74,
          "end": 259.16,
          "en": "But once we add this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.16,
          "end": 260.79,
          "en": "this error goes away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.79,
          "end": 263.05,
          "en": "because now we are creating a ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.05,
          "end": 266.42,
          "en": "which will eventually be connected to an HTMLInputElement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.308,
          "end": 269.23,
          "en": "but which has no initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.23,
          "end": 271.61,
          "en": "And we have to be explicit about this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.61,
          "end": 273.55,
          "en": "in case of useRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.55,
          "end": 277.17,
          "en": "And that's how you then create a ref when using TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.17,
          "end": 280.57,
          "en": "and how you then connect it to an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.57,
          "end": 283.313,
          "en": "And that then again just works as you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.23,
          "end": 286.086,
          "en": "Now, inside of the submitHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.086,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "we can, of course, get the enteredText",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 295.52,
          "en": "by referring to the todoTextInputRef.current.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.58,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "That's how we always do it for refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 299.6,
          "en": "They always have this current property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.6,
          "end": 301.813,
          "en": "which then holds the actual value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.72,
          "end": 304.9,
          "en": "Dot, and now the great thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.9,
          "end": 309.16,
          "en": "is that since we explicitly set this ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.16,
          "end": 310.74,
          "en": "to hold an InputElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.74,
          "end": 314.94,
          "en": "an HTMLInputElement, we get great autocompletion here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 314.94,
          "end": 319.89,
          "en": "And we get all those input element object properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.89,
          "end": 321.35,
          "en": "as suggestions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.35,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "So all the properties input element objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 326.49,
          "en": "can have in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.49,
          "end": 327.9,
          "en": "And hence, we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.9,
          "end": 331.33299999999997,
          "en": "also get this value autosuggestion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 332.68,
          "end": 334.81,
          "en": "You will notice this question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 334.81,
          "end": 336.48,
          "en": "after current though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 336.48,
          "end": 339.723,
          "en": "which in my case was added automatically by the IDE.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341,
          "end": 342.863,
          "en": "Where is this coming from?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 344.1,
          "end": 348.65,
          "en": "This question mark was added automatically by my IDE here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 348.65,
          "end": 353.65,
          "en": "because the ref is not necessarily set to a value yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.45,
          "end": 356.563,
          "en": "when we use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 357.4,
          "end": 359.24,
          "en": "Of course, here as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.24,
          "end": 362.32,
          "en": "we know that when the submitHandler is called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.32,
          "end": 366.9,
          "en": "todoTextInputRef will be connected to an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.9,
          "end": 370.06,
          "en": "because this function can only be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.06,
          "end": 371.57,
          "en": "when this form was submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.57,
          "end": 373.66,
          "en": "and that form can only be submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 373.66,
          "end": 376.173,
          "en": "after this ref was connected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.25,
          "end": 378.71,
          "en": "But of course, theoretically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 378.71,
          "end": 382.09,
          "en": "I could also try to extract a value right here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 382.09,
          "end": 383.59,
          "en": "after defining this ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 383.59,
          "end": 386.98,
          "en": "and in that case, the ref would not be connected yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 386.98,
          "end": 390.87,
          "en": "And TypeScript doesn't deeply analyze our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 390.87,
          "end": 394.55,
          "en": "it doesn't know that this technically can't be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 394.55,
          "end": 396.773,
          "en": "before this connection's established.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 397.72,
          "end": 402.17,
          "en": "In that case, this question mark addition here signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 402.17,
          "end": 405.55,
          "en": "to TypeScript that it tries to access value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 405.55,
          "end": 407.26,
          "en": "and if that succeeds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.26,
          "end": 411.21,
          "en": "the entered value will be stored in enteredText",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 411.21,
          "end": 412.83,
          "en": "but if that fails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 412.83,
          "end": 415.35,
          "en": "if the connection should not be established yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 415.35,
          "end": 418.81600000000003,
          "en": "null will be stored in enteredText.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 418.81600000000003,
          "end": 422.71,
          "en": "And that's why here the inferred type of enteredText",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 422.71,
          "end": 426.53,
          "en": "actually also is string or undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 426.53,
          "end": 428.883,
          "en": "which is basically the same as null here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 430.15,
          "end": 433.38,
          "en": "So that means that TypeScript doesn't necessarily know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 433.38,
          "end": 436.563,
          "en": "that it will be able to extract this value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 437.75,
          "end": 440.79,
          "en": "Now, if you as a developer are sure though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 440.79,
          "end": 442.66,
          "en": "that at this point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 442.66,
          "end": 445.88,
          "en": "there will be a non-null value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 445.88,
          "end": 448.38,
          "en": "so here, in this case, you know that the connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 448.38,
          "end": 449.97,
          "en": "has been established,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 449.97,
          "end": 454.25,
          "en": "you can use an exclamation mark instead of a question mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 454.25,
          "end": 457.48,
          "en": "This special annotation tells TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 457.48,
          "end": 461.84000000000003,
          "en": "that you know that this possibly nullish value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 461.84000000000003,
          "end": 465.2,
          "en": "will never be null in this spot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 465.2,
          "end": 466.24,
          "en": "And therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 466.24,
          "end": 468.28,
          "en": "you should only use this annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 468.28,
          "end": 472.73,
          "en": "if you are 100% sure that this can't be null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 472.73,
          "end": 473.7,
          "en": "So in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 473.7,
          "end": 476.86,
          "en": "that this connection will have been established.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 476.86,
          "end": 478.81,
          "en": "And then the inferred type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 478.81,
          "end": 482.34,
          "en": "is just string, not string or defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 482.34,
          "end": 483.795,
          "en": "because you are sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 483.795,
          "end": 487.37,
          "en": "that the connection will always be established",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 487.37,
          "end": 491.67,
          "en": "and that extracting the value will therefore always succeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 491.67,
          "end": 494.27,
          "en": "And we can definitely do that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 494.27,
          "end": 497.54,
          "en": "since we know that technically submitHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 497.54,
          "end": 499.4,
          "en": "the way we write our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 499.4,
          "end": 502.81,
          "en": "can't be called before this line of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 502.81,
          "end": 507.44,
          "en": "was parsed and this connection was therefore established.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 507.44,
          "end": 509.36,
          "en": "But that is an important concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 509.36,
          "end": 513.383,
          "en": "which I definitely also wanted to briefly explore here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 514.24,
          "end": 516.29,
          "en": "Now, it is worth pointing out though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 516.29,
          "end": 518.42,
          "en": "that these question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 518.42,
          "end": 521.48,
          "en": "and exclamation mark operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 521.48,
          "end": 525.44,
          "en": "are not related to refs specifically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 525.44,
          "end": 528.64,
          "en": "This is also not a React-specific feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 528.64,
          "end": 531.26,
          "en": "Instead, these are regular operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 531.26,
          "end": 533.55,
          "en": "which you can use in TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 533.55,
          "end": 537.74,
          "en": "when you are working with values that could be null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 537.74,
          "end": 541.23,
          "en": "With question mark, you're always saying try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 541.23,
          "end": 543.42,
          "en": "to get me that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 543.42,
          "end": 547.24,
          "en": "and if it's null, store null in the constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 547.24,
          "end": 550.07,
          "en": "or wherever I wanna store that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 550.07,
          "end": 551.5,
          "en": "With the exclamation mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 551.5,
          "end": 555.04,
          "en": "you're saying I'm certain that here we won't be dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 555.889,
          "end": 558.09,
          "en": "with null, so therefore, drill into this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 558.09,
          "end": 559.27,
          "en": "into this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 559.27,
          "end": 563.4,
          "en": "and give me the actual stored non-null value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 563.4,
          "end": 566.16,
          "en": "and therefore then you will always get that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 566.16,
          "end": 567.64,
          "en": "But of course, as explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 567.64,
          "end": 570.22,
          "en": "that only works if you are certain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 570.22,
          "end": 572.09,
          "en": "that this can't be null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 572.09,
          "end": 575.28,
          "en": "So these are two generally important operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 575.28,
          "end": 578.83,
          "en": "in TypeScript, which here are very important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 578.83,
          "end": 580.46,
          "en": "when working with refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 580.46,
          "end": 584.18,
          "en": "since refs could be null or could not be connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 584.18,
          "end": 586.847,
          "en": "to any value at this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 586.847,
          "end": 590.054,
          "en": "And with that, we've now got the enteredText",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 590.054,
          "end": 592.33,
          "en": "and we could now validate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 592.33,
          "end": 594.424,
          "en": "and check if enteredText,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 594.424,
          "end": 598.283,
          "en": "once we trim it maybe is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 599.17,
          "end": 601.69,
          "en": "which would mean that nothing was entered in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 601.69,
          "end": 603.293,
          "en": "just a bunch of blanks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 605.61,
          "end": 607.66,
          "en": "Or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 607.66,
          "end": 610.22,
          "en": "So here we could throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 610.22,
          "end": 612.083,
          "en": "I'll just return though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 613.47,
          "end": 615.17,
          "en": "If we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 615.17,
          "end": 617.57,
          "en": "we know that we have a valid input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 617.57,
          "end": 618.87,
          "en": "and just to make this clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 618.87,
          "end": 621.82,
          "en": "this is not about whether the ref is connected or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 621.82,
          "end": 625.22,
          "en": "this is just validating the text entered by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 625.22,
          "end": 627.253,
          "en": "which has nothing to do with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 628.21,
          "end": 630.41,
          "en": "But once we made it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 630.41,
          "end": 633.05,
          "en": "we now wanna add that todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 633.05,
          "end": 634.8,
          "en": "to our list of todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 634.8,
          "end": 637.65,
          "en": "And we probably don't do this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 637.65,
          "end": 641.456,
          "en": "inside of our NewTodo component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 641.456,
          "end": 644.24,
          "en": "Instead, we're managing the list of todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 644.24,
          "end": 646.1,
          "en": "in the App component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 646.1,
          "end": 648.65,
          "en": "and hence, we'll need a way of communicating back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 648.65,
